                <pb facs="0250" n="154" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg154"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Pekin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-06-11"><hi rendition="#italic">June 11,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Prince Tuan, father Heir-Apparent, has been appointed president of the Tsungli
                    Yamen, with three other new ministers, all greatly opposed to foreigners.
                    Situation not improved. Seven hundred additional guards repairing railway en
                    route. Their arrival will assure safety foreigners here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Conger.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
